# Generated outputs. Both a local run and the scheduled Actions run rewrite
# these wholesale, so git's line-level merge produces a conflict in the middle
# of a JSON document — thousands of lines of noise for a file that is simply
# regenerated on the next run.
#
# `-merge` marks them unmergeable: git still reports the conflict, but leaves
# the two versions whole so resolving is `git checkout --theirs <file>` rather
# than hand-editing JSON.
data/news.json          -merge
data/rejected.json      -merge
site/news.json          -merge
data/cache/seen.json    -merge
data/cache/summaries.json -merge
data/cache/usage.json   -merge
data/cache/gnews_urls.json -merge

# Keep line endings sane across a Windows dev box and Linux CI runners.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
